"prose": [
{
"from": 202,
"to": 209,
"text": "No boot path is touched: no binary, stand boot or session code changes, so there is no `smoke` entry. The chunk has no Rust delta, so the local pre-push gate's cargo legs read the tree as the previous chunk left it. The gates are: - the `ci-scripts` leg, which holds the widened pin; - the audit over the edited `deny.toml`; - four text probes: the stale strings, the retired owner file, the leaves' stale counts, and the secret search; - the preservation guard; - the local pre-push gate; - the operator pass's CI read."
},
{
"from": 211,
"to": 215,
"text": "The pin's control is implement's one-shot `gate.py control`, never an entry. Fired on the `ci-scripts` entry, it deletes the word `--test open_state ` from `.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh`'s stand-repeat list. Its case is `test_the_leg_counts_are_stated_in_words`, which reads failed (seventeen becomes sixteen against the page), then the restored tree reads green. `--timeout 300` covers the leg's ~12 s. A timeout would read held, so the run's own `failed` line is what decides."
}
],
